<title>BRAZIL: Brazilian soybean and product market.</title>
<headline>Brazilian soybean and product market.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brokers reported the following Brazilian soybean and products basis levels.</p>
<p>(NB - no buyer T-Trade P-Premium D-Discount)</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	   BASIS	 MONTH		PREV</p>
<p>Soybean (cents per bushel)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> April	     15/8 D	 April		10/8 D</p>
<p> May		20/13 D	 May		  10/8 D</p>
<p> July	    2 D/even	 July		  4/7 P</p>
<p> August	  even/3 P	 August	    10/13 P</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	   BASIS	 MONTH	   PREV</p>
<p>Soymeal/Pellets (dollars per short tonne 48 pct profat)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> April		4/2 D	 March		 4/2 D</p>
<p> May	    16.5/15 D	 May	     16.5/15 D</p>
<p> July	     18/17 D	 July		18/17 D</p>
<p> August	    10/6 D	 August	     10/6 D</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	   BASIS	 MONTH	   PREV</p>
<p>Soybean Oil (dollars per tonne, points per lb, crude, degummed)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> April	  170/100 D	 April	   170/n/a D</p>
<p> May	    210/130 D	 May	     200/150 D</p>
<p> July	   220/180 D	 July	    215/185 D</p>
<p> August	 200/180 D	 August	  200/180 D</p>
